# Purpose and audience: executable specification evidence for the owning engineering team.
# @req REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
# research: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; design: doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md

"""
## Purpose and audience

Purpose: pin that `use m.{f as g}` binds `g` to `m`'s `f` under NATIVE/AOT
codegen even when the importing module also declares its own `fn f`.
Audience: compiler engineers maintaining HIR lowering and native mangling.

## Operator workflow

1. Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/compiler/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_spec.spl`.
2. Every scenario must pass; a failure is a regression in alias resolution.

## Compatibility and limitations

Exercises the seed's native-project lane (`SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_RUST=1`).
Set `SIMPLE_BIN` to target a specific binary; default `bin/simple`.
"""

# doc-path: doc/01_research/local/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_spec.md
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/sys_test/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_spec.md
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_spec.md
# doc-path: doc/05_design/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_spec_oracles.md
# @manual: primary

"""
# Aliased import must outrank a same-named local definition (AOT lane)

Bug: doc/08_tracking/bug/aliased_import_shadowed_by_local_fn_native_codegen_2026-09-03.md

`use other.{probe as aliased_probe}` inside a module that ALSO defines
`fn probe` used to lower, under native codegen, to a call to the LOCAL
`probe`. When the local `probe` was itself the caller the emitted function
called ITSELF -- measured as `main__probe` carrying
`IMAGE_REL_AMD64_REL32 main__probe`, with ZERO relocation to
`other__probe` -- and the process died with a stack overflow
(`0xC00000FD`, which MSYS bash renders as exit 127). Four stdlib modules
hit this; it corrupted native builds on EVERY platform.

**This spec must shell out and assert at the OBJECT level.** The
interpreter was always CORRECT here (it consults `import_alias_bindings`,
populated only on the flattened lane), so an in-process assertion is green
on a broken compiler. The failure mode is also a stack overflow, which a
runner reports as an opaque non-zero exit -- so running the binary is not a
usable oracle either.

Oracle: in the ENTRY module's object, a reference to `other__probe` proves
the alias reached the imported function; a reference to `main__probe`
proves the same module's own local calls still bind locally. Both must
hold at once -- fixing one direction by breaking the other is not a fix.

Fail-closed: if no entry object is produced, the scenarios FAIL. A run that
inspected nothing must never read as a pass.
"""
use std.spec.step

use std.spipe.*
use std.io.{process_run, env_get}

fn simple_binary() -> text:
    val configured = env_get("SIMPLE_BIN") ?? ""
    if configured.len() > 0:
        return configured
    "bin/simple"

fn probe_script() -> text:
    "test/fixtures/aliased_import/probe_alias_binding.sh"

fn probe_output() -> text:
    val (stdout, stderr, _code) = process_run("sh", [probe_script(), simple_binary()])
    stdout + stderr

describe "aliased import outranks a same-named local definition under native codegen":
    # @manual scenario evidence

    it "produces an entry object to inspect (fail-closed, never a vacuous pass)":
        # @req: REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
        step("Verify: the native lane emitted the entry module's object")
        expect(probe_output()).to_contain("ENTRY_OBJECT=found")

    it "binds the alias to the IMPORTED function, not the local one":
        # @req: REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
        step("Verify: the entry object references other__probe")
        # Pre-fix ground truth: this reference was ABSENT and the call
        # relocated to main__probe -- the function calling itself.
        expect(probe_output()).to_contain("ALIAS_TARGET=imported")

    it "still binds a same-module local call to the LOCAL definition":
        # @req: REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
        step("Verify: the entry object still references main__probe")
        # Opposite direction: suppressing the alias rewrite must not
        # detach ordinary local calls from their own module's function.
        expect(probe_output()).to_contain("LOCAL_SYMBOL=present")
